  "adaptation": "Port the official capture timing, fade curves, renderer selection and Z sort. Replace Framework.DependencyInjection RenderTexturePool with a battle-scope RTHandle pool preserving the 5 MiB active allocation limit, 128-pixel clamp, RGBA8 format, point filtering, clamp wrapping and disposal at scope end. Instantiate the authored RTRenderer prefab directly; bind the pool through the native battle playable scope.",
  "runtime_validation": "Unity import, compilation and Zjcs.Editor.ProjectTools.Validate passed. Windowed original 13970 Play Mode passed native body/appearance mesh selection, four original 300x300 GPU captures (7817/8019/8160/8160 nontransparent pixels), original fade colors, actual visible afterimages, simulated original start/leave input, damage/checkpoint/result and returned capture resources. Runtime screenshots were inspected. Scripts-only Windows build and actual internal-display Player passed the same original graph, four nonempty native GPU captures, fade colors, visible afterimages, simulated start/leave input, damage/checkpoint/result and returned capture resources; all six Player images were inspected. Other afterimage graphs and native monster capture remain unverified."
